+/**
+ * PowerPC vector support.
+ *
+ * The "ppc64" kernel only requires the AltiVec (VMX) instructions found in
+ * the PowerPC G4, G5, and POWER6 or better, so it can be used on both 32-bit
+ * and 64-bit PowerPC, as long as the compiler targets AltiVec (e.g., with
+ * -maltivec, -mcpu=G4, -mcpu=970 or -mcpu=power8). When the compiler also
+ * targets the POWER8 vector facilities (VSX unaligned loads and stores,
